^SERIES = GSE149341
!Series_title = RNA-seq of control and USP7 siRNA transfected ES and 2-cell like cells
!Series_geo_accession = GSE149341
!Series_status = Public on Jan 18 2022
!Series_submission_date = Apr 25 2020
!Series_last_update_date = Feb 22 2022
!Series_summary = 2-cell-like cells (2CLCs) that resemble 2-cell stage embryos can arise with a very low frequency in ES cell cultures. Here, we found a novel factor, Usp7 which promotes 2CLC transition from ESCs and its effect is dependent of DNA replication. Endogenous retroviruses and 2-cell stage specific genes are significantly upregulated in siUSP7-transfected 2CLCs.
!Series_overall_design = RNA-seq of siControl and siUSP7 transfected cells. GFP+ are 2CLCs.
!Series_type = Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing
